 \subsection{Axiom 7: Informational vectors and derived per-atom metrics}
 \label{subsec:axiom_v1_metrics}
+\Needspace{7\baselineskip}
+\emph{A map of this axiom.} Each quantity below is defined in the text, in this order, and none enters a verb unless it is named.
+{\footnotesize
+\begin{longtable}[c]{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{4.4cm}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{6.4cm}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{3.4cm}@{}}
+\hline
+Quantity & What it answers & Range \\ \hline
+\endhead
+vector $v_i=(r_i,\hat n_i,\chi_i)$, sort $\tau_i$ & One informational reading, an instance of Axiom~1 & $0<r_i\le1$ \\
+core; $N$, $Q$, $D$ & Cores, vectors, distinct cores; each vector is in one core, and the grouping is part of the atom & $Q\ge0$, $D\le N$ \\
+$V_{\text{derived}}=\sum r_i\hat n_i$ & The raw sum of the vectors; a meta vector, uncapped and not normalized & any length \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{str}}$ & How much strength in total & $\ge0$ \\
+atom coherence $\lvert V_{\text{derived}}\rvert/\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{str}}$ & How far the vectors reinforce one another & $[0,1]$ \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{vol}}$, $\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{mean}}$ & Total and per-vector volume ($r^3$) & $<\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{str}}$ if some $r_i<1$ \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{en}}$ & Squared magnitude if all vectors were orthogonal & $\ge0$ \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{agr}}$ & Whether the directions agree or cancel (weighted mean cosine) & $[-1,1]$ \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{vcon}}$ & How unevenly volume is shared among vectors & $[0,1]$ \\
+$\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{scon}}(w)$ & Whether many vectors share one strength bin of width $w$ & $[0,1]$ \\
+$Q_{\mathrm{eff}}=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{str}}^2/\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{en}}$ & Equally strong vectors that carry the same energy & $[1,Q]$ \\ \hline
+\end{longtable}}
+\addtocounter{table}{-1}
 The teaching atom of \hyperref[subsec:axiom1]{Axiom~1} is one unit
 ($N=Q=1$), one state among several. An atom may also be \emph{Collapsed}: $Q$ informational
 vectors $v_i=(r_i,\hat n_i,\chi_i)$, each carrying its own phase-color $\chi_i\in[0,2\pi)$ alongside $(r_i,\hat n_i)$ and its own sort $\tau_i$ --- $v_i$ together with $\tau_i$ forming, per vector, the same unit \hyperref[subsec:axiom1]{Axiom~1} states, still capped at $r_i\le 1$, and positive: a vector of strength zero is black
